version: "3.1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-24"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  Qali (called LiNaK until November 2026) is an open-source Python toolkit, with a desktop
  interface, for the atomic structure and light-matter properties of the alkali atoms Li to Fr
  and alkali-like ions. It combines NIST Atomic Spectra Database levels with quantum-defect
  theory and model-potential wavefunctions, and adds its own Dirac-Hartree-Fock calculation
  with core polarisation and second- and third-order Brueckner corrections. From these it
  computes energy levels, E1 matrix elements and oscillator strengths, radiative and blackbody
  lifetimes, static and dynamic polarisabilities, magic wavelengths, optical-tweezer traps and
  scattering rates, hyperfine and Zeeman structure, Feshbach resonances and absorption spectra.
  For Rydberg states it gives Stark maps in static and oscillating fields (Shirley's Floquet
  method), dipole-dipole pair potentials, C3 and C6 coefficients and blockade radii, checked
  against measurements and against ARC. Results come as interactive pages and as
  publication-ready figures, with optional bridges to ORCA and ARC.
